{{- /*
Resolve whether Homebrew is used on this machine.

Deliberately independent of is-root. Having sudo says nothing about wanting
Homebrew: a locked-down work machine may well grant sudo for apt while having no
business running linuxbrew, and the two were previously welded together behind a
single is_root flag.

macOS defaults to true, since Homebrew is the norm there. Linux defaults to
false and is opt-in per machine, so a sudo-capable Linux box gets apt packages
and nothing else unless it asks for brew.

Resolution order:
  1. DOTFILES_HOMEBREW environment override
  2. use_homebrew persisted in chezmoi.toml by a previous init
  3. true on macOS, false on Linux

Returns the string "true" or "false".

Usage: {{ if eq (includeTemplate "use-homebrew" . | trim) "true" }}
*/ -}}
{{- $override := env "DOTFILES_HOMEBREW" -}}
{{- if eq $override "true" -}}
{{-   "true" -}}
{{- else if eq $override "false" -}}
{{-   "false" -}}
{{- else if $override -}}
{{-   fail (printf "DOTFILES_HOMEBREW must be \"true\" or \"false\", got %q" $override) -}}
{{- else if hasKey . "use_homebrew" -}}
{{-   if .use_homebrew }}true{{ else }}false{{ end -}}
{{- else if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" -}}
{{-   "true" -}}
{{- else -}}
{{-   "false" -}}
{{- end -}}
